> 6. **[r3] Recorded-before-deadline wins (F016.2).** `resume_on` (`wait_commit.rs`) and the wait
>    sweeper consume a matching unconsumed event whose `created_at <= wait.deadline` before
>    deciding expiry: such a wait completes with that event even when the resume runs after the
>    deadline; only a wait with no such event expires. This applies to every `wait.event` (it is the
>    same contract for any producer) and is covered by a test where the event is recorded just
>    before the deadline and the resume runs after it. Run-deadline expiry (`expire_on`) is
>    unchanged: a run past its own deadline fails, and its unconsumed events stay unconsumed.
> 7. **[r3] Allowlist channels (F016.3).** A member replying by email to a `user` send passes
>    ingress through the existing thread-party fallback: `authorize_channel` consults
>    `thread_access_for` whenever the channel ACL refuses an external sender
>    (`routing.rs:325-343`), and `thread_access_for` returns `Participant` for a party of the
>    ancestor thread, which D1.5.4 makes the member for the thread the send opened. The channel's
>    allowlist therefore does not bounce it. Test: allowlist run channel, unlisted member, user send,
>    email reply → accepted and matched.
